{
 "_doc": "Stream C (owner feedback 10, Y32): classes that exist ONLY in Thousandvale, injected in memory at engine boot by js/rules/tv-skills.js `installTvClasses` (Farhold's classes.json and skills.json are shared with live games and are never written). `classes` = whole class rows in Farhold's classes.json shape (plus `tv: true`, `outfit` = the class-outfit id D-world dresses it with, `resourceName` = its signature resource). `skills` = its skill rows in Farhold's skills.json shape, each with a four-tier talent tree (2 bespoke nodes + one shared library node a tier, every node a rule); a row's `tv.sky` = { proj, fallMs } makes each of its ground strikes a star that FALLS: the rules send fx `skyfall` (to, r, ms, proj) `fallMs` before the strike so the client can draw it coming down. The Starcaller's signature is the resource `starlight` (Farhold's own resource mechanic: 5 at most): Star Dart and Scattered Stars gain 1 for each enemy hit, Called Star / Star Field / Heavens' Barrage spend all of it (`perPoint.mult` more damage a point) and change at five (`atMax`). Projectile kinds are named in data/rules/projectiles.json (`star` for the two thrown skills, `skystar` for what falls). Kits are in data/rules/starter-kits.json, the themed armour in data/rules/armour-tiers.json. ROUND 11 (Z52/Z55, owner #53/#56): the Star Blade (`starblade`) — the Starcaller's melee partner, same `starlight` resource spent differently: gained by melee hits (Starcut / Star Tether / Comet Rush), by hits TAKEN (`tv.hurtGain` { id, n, every seconds, fromLevel }) and by each blow Star Aegis answers (its `counter.gain`); spent on defence and control. `tv.points` = what each point spent adds besides damage (`barrier` share of maximum health, `answer` x the counter's answer, `hold` seconds on the skill's roots) and `atMax.stun` (seconds, a stun on what it hits/answers at five) — js/rules/cast-skills.js `applyPoints`, card text js/rules/wording.js.",
